WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.580
Oh!

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.950
Huh?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.510
Greg?

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Did you fetch for me the Golden comb?

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.510
Will that work?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.510
This is a honeycomb.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:41.430
Golden comb of honey, yee-he-he-he.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.430
Greg! Oh!

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.010
Oh!

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.520
Gre-e-e-e-g!

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:47.520
Huh?

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.520
Never mind that, Gregory.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.400
You've brought me the first two items...

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.600
a golden comb and a spool of silver thread.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.410
It's just spider web on a stick.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.700
Now, I want the sun.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.120
The sun?

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.220
Here.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.210
Lower the sun out of the sky

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.620
and into this China cup.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.630
Uh, well, that sounds impossible.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:10.910
Anything is possible if you set your mind to it, right?

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.880
But hurry, the sun will be setting soon, and-

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.590
Hey, yeah, that's it.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.800
♪ Duh dih-dunh ♪
♪ dunh-dunh din-dunh ♪

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.800
♪ duh din-din dunh ♪

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:25.100
See, that old sun's going
right down into this old cup.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.690
You have figured it out, and I thought you might give up.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.770
Give up? I'll never give up.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.280
♪ Just got to wait, just got to wait. ♪

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.280
Yes, just sit there in the cold and wait.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.950
Huh?

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.120
Ohh...

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:48.880
What the...

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:49.880
Ohh. Ohh.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:50.500
Beatrice?!

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.880
Huh?! Wirt!

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:52.880
Beatrice!

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.300
What are you doing out here?!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.300
I saw Greg!

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:55.970
What?!

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:56.970
I saw Greg.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.970
He was... with someone.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:01:59.970
This way!

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.300
Or wait. Um...

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.390
Beatrice, you should go home.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.390
I can't ... not yet.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.270
Not until Greg is safe.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.270
Okay.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.610
We should hurry.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.610
I... I think it was that way.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.610
Thank you, Beatrice.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.640
Oh! Ohh...

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.120
Huh!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.400
Here! Edelwood!

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.880
You see? This will give us some oil, won't it?

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.550
Yes, we'll keep that light of yours shining, won't we?

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.550
Come on.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.550
Aw! You...

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.930
♪ Come wayward souls ♪

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.550
Oh!

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.720
♪ Who wander through the darkness ♪

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:56.690
♪ There is a light for the lost and the meek ♪

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.810
♪ Sorrow and fear ♪

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.990
♪ are easily forgotten ♪

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:16.340
♪ when you submit
to the soil of the Earth ♪

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.630
Woodsman, I knew you would come.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.430
I have something for you.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.430
Huh! Ah!
What have you done?!

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.770
Why, I've given you another edelwood.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:28.770
No!

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.100
He will burn nicely in the lantern.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.860
No! I won't do this!

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.440
You've been grinding up lost souls for years!

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.230
I didn't know!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:42.030
I didn't know this is where the edelwood trees came from!

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.610
And would it have mattered?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.620
Would you have just let your daughter's spirit burn out forever?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.790
Feed the lantern.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.370
No...

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:53.600
I suppose, after all these years,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.210
you just don't care for her anymore.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:58.380
Hold your tongue, or I'll remove it from your mouth!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.980
Do not speak of my daughter.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.980
She would not wish this.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.050
Let's get you free.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:08.060
Ah!

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.390
I only wish to help you, woodsman.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.480
You need oil, or else your daughter will...

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.840
I told you to hold your tongue!

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.320
Ha! Ha! Ha! Ha!

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.320
Greg? Greg!

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.490
I thought it was this way.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.660
A light.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.250
A lantern.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.670
It looks like the woodsman's.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.240
♪ Oh Potatus ♪

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:42.090
- Whoa. What happened here?
- Greg!

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.170
♪ et Molassus ♪

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.170
Greg!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:51.250
♪ Si Velis eis quaere a nobis ♪

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:44.260
Are you...

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.260
Wirt?

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.430
Oh, Greg!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.340
Wirt, I did it!

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.850
I beat the beast.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:59.280
♪ Lenes et caldi valuti catuli ♪

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.770
Aw, geez, the leaves are even growing inside of him.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.440
No, I was just eating leaves.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.770
I'm sorry, Wirt.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:06.420
♪ Pleni cum petri dulcibus ♪

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.780
No, no, Greg.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.080
It's my fault we ended up here.
Everything's been my fault.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.110
I-I should have been more...

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:14.220
♪ Oh Potatus et Molassus ♪

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.480
No, I mean...

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.540
my rock facts rock.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.450
- What?!
- What?!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.450
I ... I stole it, Wirt.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.320
I stole it from Mrs. Daniel's garden.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:23.300
♪ Si Velis eis quaere a nobis ♪

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.130
I'm a stealer.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.800
And that's a rock fact.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.070
What?! No,

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.550
Greg, that doesn't matter.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:31.170
♪ Lenes et caldi valuti catuli ♪

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.030
I does matter.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.800
You have to return it for me, okay?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.810
No, you can give it to her yourself!

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:31.760
Come on,

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:39.650
♪ Potatus et Molassus ♪

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:32.810
w-we got to get...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.810
Jason Funderberker home, right?

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.860
Jason Funderberker...

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:41.070
the perfect... frog name.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.070
Greg? Greg?!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:50.150
♪ Grow, tiny seed, ♪

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.070
Let's get him out of this! Come on!

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.660
Yeah. Yeah...

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.040
Come on!

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.790
It's gonna be fine, Wirt.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:56.910
♪ you are called to the trees... ♪

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.580
Ohh...

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.750
Give me my lantern.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.640
Your lantern?

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.020
No way. We need this thing.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.250
Yeah, I'm keeping this.
I have to get Greg home.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.510
Your brother is too weak to go home.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.760
He will soon become part of my forest.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.090
I won't let that happen!

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.090
Well, then...

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.430
perhaps we better make a deal.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.430
Deal?

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:16.850
Ohh...

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.480
I can put his spirit in the lantern.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.610
As long as the flame stays lit,
he will live on inside.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.780
Take on the task of lantern bearer...

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.950
or watch your brother perish.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.700
Come here.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.700
Okay.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.370
Wirt!

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.380
Wait...

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.210
That's dumb.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.040
What?

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:43.750
That's dumb.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.470
I'm not just gonna just wander around in the woods

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.550
for the rest of my life.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.380
I'm trying to help you.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.780
You're not trying to help me.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.740
You just have some weird obsession with keeping this lantern lit.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.040
I-It's almost like...

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.560
your soul is in this lantern.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:04.480
Are you ready to see true darkness?

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.150
Are yo... Ahem

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.160
Are you?

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.200
Don't! Don't!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.370
Here, woodsman.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.170
I've got my own problems to take care of.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.750
This one's yours.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.280
My brother and I are going home.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:33.640
She was never in the lantern,
was she, beast?

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:37.640
Listen, woodsman!
Listen to me.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:40.810
Wirt...

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.600
Come with us.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.980
I... I got to go home, too.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.150
admit to my family it's my fault they're bluebirds.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:50.320
What?!

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.740
The scissors that'll make your family human again.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.320
You had them all along?!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.180
I-I used them to escape
Adelaide, and th-then...

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.250
Yeah, I-I was sort of mad at you.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.680
Oh, you...

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.560
wonderful mistake of nature!

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.380
You see, woodsman?

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:09.880
All who perish here will become trees for the lantern.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.550
Cut them down with your ax.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.880
Go! Now!

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:15.800
No!

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.970
Stop!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:25.480
Are you really ready to go back
to that empty house?

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.240
No! Woodsman!

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.060
Goodbye, Beatrice.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.490
Goodbye, Wirt.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.660
♪ One is a bird ♪

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:41.410
♪ two are the trees ♪

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:48.170
♪ three is the wind in the leaves ♪

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.170
HELP...

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.590
-HUH! WIRT!
- WIRT!

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:52.370
♪ Four are the stars ♪

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:55.590
♪ Five with the moon ♪

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.590
WIRT? YOU OKAY?

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.350
CAN YOU SEE ME, WIRT?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.510
HMM. WHERE AM I?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:01.350
HOSPITAL.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.350
HOSP... ITAL?

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.640
GREG! WHERE'S GREG?!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.940
...AND THEN...

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:06.600
WIRT!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.930
I WAS TELLING THEM ABOUT THE
TIME WE ALMOST GOT...

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:09.420
GRAWR.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:13.070
YEAH, AND YOU WERE THERE, TOO,
JASON FUNDERBERKER.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:13.820
ME?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:14.820
NOT YOU!

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.130
JASON FUNDERBERKER, MY FROG.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:17.770
GRAWR.

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:18.740
OUR FROG.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.740
OUR FROG.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.410
OUR FROG?

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.410
NO, NOT YOUR FROG.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.080
HEY, SO... UH...

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.080
ABOUT THIS...

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.750
YEAH, SO...

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.510
I DON'T HAVE A TAPE PLAYER, SO...

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:34.420
UH, YEAH.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.180
SO MAYBE WE CAN LISTEN TO THIS...

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.720
YOU CAN LISTEN TO IT AT MY
HOUSE. YES.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.520
MAYBE... MAYBE WE SHOULD LISTEN
TO SOME OTHER TAPES FIRST, THOUGH

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.180
AND SORT OF WORK OUR WAY TO THIS ONE.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.060
THIS ONE IS A LITTLE BIT... UH...

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.360
I MEAN, Y-YOU CAN LISTEN TO IT...

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.020
And so the story is complete,

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.940
and everyone is
satisfied with the ending.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.440
And so on and so forth, and yet...

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.180
over the garden wall...

00:09:56.180 --> 00:10:00.190
♪ How the gentle wind ♪

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:04.170
♪ beckons through the leaves ♪

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.340
Father?

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:10.880
♪ as autumn colors fall ♪

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:17.090
♪ dancing in a swirl ♪

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:21.180
♪ of golden memories ♪

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:27.890
♪ the loveliest lies of all ♪

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.440
Honey, eat your dirt.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:45.910
Mom, stop calling it dirt.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.910
What are you gonna do about it?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.580
turn us into bluebirds again?

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.250
Mom...

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.340
Now, eat your dirt.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:11:06.680
♪ the loveliest lies of all. ♪

